  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental funds only (no enterprise funds); business_type null. Basic statement figures from p4 (Statement of Cash Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Cash Basis Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column). Identity: 4,427,820 + 6,751,560 - 6,064,418 + 1,278,180 - 1,278,180 = 5,114,962. Ending cash 5,114,962 includes investments of 784,505 (p1, p3), so ending_investments left null. Balance sheet from p1 Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (no liabilities). Transfer cross-check: General out 1,128,180 = Road in 1,120,469 + 911 Emergency in 5,000 + 911 Wireless in 2,711; Road out 150,000 = Road Sinking in 150,000; total in/out 1,278,180 each (p4). General Fund disbursements (3,293,156) equal the statement, so no transfers hidden in spending lines. Detail: General Fund (p5) departmental budget schedule used; Road, Inheritance Tax, Highway Buyback (pp6-7) are one-line disbursements. The 18 nonmajor funds are recorded using the combining schedule Total Nonmajor column (p16) per the more-than-6-funds rule; the per-fund budget schedules pp8-11 (Road Sinking, Visitors Promotion, Visitors Improvement, Preservation, Vets Aid, Opioid, Diversion, Drug, K-9, COVID ARP, Local Assistance, 911 Emergency, 911 Wireless, Juvenile Justice, Hospital Bond, Road Bond, Highway Allocation Bond, Keno) and combining pages pp12-15 are not repeated to avoid double counting. Taxes line split by fund column: Inheritance Tax Fund 107,008 as inheritance tax; the remaining 3,742,892 (General and Nonmajor) is not broken down anywhere and stays taxes (unlabeled). Road and Inheritance Tax one-line DISBURSEMENTS (p6) are split by function using their p4 fund columns (Road: public works 1,706,009 + capital outlay 180,401; Inheritance: general government 179,901 + capital outlay 12,779). Noxious weed control (listed under Public Works on p5) categorized natural resources/conservation in detail. Statement 'Public Works' mapped to streets/highways. Read pages 1-16 of 16."
